{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.FlatTransport","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.FlatTransport","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.LinearODE","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.ODE.Gronwall","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.MeanValue","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.MetricSpace.Thickening","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.UniformSpace.HeineCantor","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Convex.Star"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.flat_transport_eq_of_endpoints","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.flat_transport_eq_of_endpoints","kind":"theorem","line":476,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L476-L490","doc":"Transport between two points of a flat star-shaped domain does not depend on the path. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.flat_transport_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.flat_transport_eq","kind":"theorem","line":452,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L452-L474","doc":"**Path independence of flat transport.**  On an open domain `D`, star-shaped about `c`,\non which `ω` is flat, transport along any `C¹` path `γ` in `D` satisfies\n`U(1) · Φ(γ 0) = Φ(γ 1)`, where `Φ = radialTransport ω c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.isUnit_radialTransport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.isUnit_radialTransport","kind":"theorem","line":442,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L442-L450","doc":"Radial transport is invertible at every point of a star-shaped domain. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.seg_mem_of_starConvex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.seg_mem_of_starConvex","kind":"theorem","line":435,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L435-L440","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.hasFDerivAt_radialTransport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.hasFDerivAt_radialTransport","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L197-L430","doc":"**Radial transport is differentiable**, with `DΦ(x) h = ω(x)(h) · Φ(x)`, at every `x`\nwhose segment from `c` lies in the open set `D` on which `ω` is flat. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.norm_le_of_dist_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.norm_le_of_dist_lt","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L190-L194","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.mul_le_half_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.mul_le_half_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L181-L188","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.continuousOn_transportCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.continuousOn_transportCoeff","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L171-L177","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.continuousOn_radialX","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.continuousOn_radialX","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L162-L168","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.radialTransport_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.radialTransport_eq","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L155-L159","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.IsFundSol.eqOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.IsFundSol.eqOn","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L151-L153","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.radialTransport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.radialTransport","kind":"def","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L144-L148","doc":"Radial transport from `c` to `x` (equal to `1` when the coefficient is not continuous,\nwhich never happens for `x` in a star-shaped domain of a connection). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.radialX","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.radialX","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L139-L140","doc":"The coefficient of the transport equation along the segment from `c` to `x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.IsTransport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.IsTransport","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L135-L137","doc":"`U` is the parallel transport of `ω` along the path `γ` with velocity `γ'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.IsFlatOn.flat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.IsFlatOn.flat","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L133-L133","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.IsFlatOn.continuousOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.IsFlatOn.continuousOn","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L132-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.IsFlatOn.hasFDerivAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.IsFlatOn.hasFDerivAt","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L131-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.IsFlatOn.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.IsFlatOn.mk","kind":"ctor","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L130-L130","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.IsFlatOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.IsFlatOn","kind":"structure","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L127-L133","doc":"`ω` is a flat connection form on `D` with derivative `ω'` (`ω' y a = ∂_a ω` at `y`):\ndifferentiable with continuous derivative on `D`, and with vanishing curvature\n`∂_a ω_b − ∂_b ω_a − [ω_a, ω_b] = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.norm_le_of_linear_defect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.norm_le_of_linear_defect","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L103-L123","doc":"Grönwall for a function whose defect against a bounded linear equation is bounded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.defect_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.defect_identity","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L87-L101","doc":"The algebraic heart of the flatness argument: the defect of\n`G = W − U − t·(b U)` against the perturbed equation is, after flatness, the sum of a term\nlinear in `d − t·L h (v+h)` and a term quadratic in `h`.  Here `P = a + b + d` stands for\n`ω(γ t + t h)(v + h)`, `a = ω(γ t) v`, `b = ω(γ t) h`, `d = Δ(v + h)` and\n`Lxy = ω'(γ t) x y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.gronwallBound_zero_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.gronwallBound_zero_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L69-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.gronwallBound_zero_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.gronwallBound_zero_eq","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L63-L67","doc":"`gronwallBound` with zero initial value is linear in the forcing term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.exists_uniform_near_compact_norm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.exists_uniform_near_compact_norm","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L55-L61","doc":"Normed-group form of `exists_uniform_near_compact`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.exists_uniform_near_compact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.exists_uniform_near_compact","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZHolonomy/FlatTransport.lean#L45-L53","doc":"A function continuous at every point of a compact set is uniformly continuous *at* that\nset, in metric form. ","signatureChunk":0}]}